1
00:00:07,512 --> 00:00:09,681
EIKICHI - AZUSA ONIZUKA

2
00:00:13,451 --> 00:00:14,886
<i>To my dearest wife.</i>

3
00:00:15,720 --> 00:00:18,890
<i>It's been two weeks since</i>
<i>you went back to your parents' home.</i>

4
00:00:19,457 --> 00:00:21,759
<i>Has anything changed with you since then?</i>

5
00:00:22,260 --> 00:00:23,461
DIVORCE FORM

6
00:00:23,528 --> 00:00:24,496
<i>As for me,</i>

7
00:00:24,562 --> 00:00:27,932
<i>one of my students</i>
<i>tried to start a new team…</i>

8
00:00:27,999 --> 00:00:30,435
It was only a short time,
but thank you for everything.

9
00:00:30,502 --> 00:00:33,304
Don't try to reset
the hard work you put in so far.

10
00:00:33,905 --> 00:00:37,308
<i>I barely managed to stop her</i>
<i>from quitting school.</i>

11
00:00:37,375 --> 00:00:40,311
<i>And as a result,</i>
<i>I got one more good rating</i>

12
00:00:40,378 --> 00:00:42,013
<i>in the feedback system.</i>

13
00:00:42,080 --> 00:00:43,014
-How about it?
-Please!

14
00:00:43,581 --> 00:00:45,450
<i>We haven't gotten new members yet,</i>

15
00:00:45,517 --> 00:00:48,219
<i>but I'll do my best</i>
<i>not to lose to the two of them.</i>

16
00:00:48,286 --> 00:00:52,390
<i>So can you come home soon,</i>
<i>so we can do drills together?</i>

17
00:00:52,457 --> 00:00:54,192
Oh, right.

18
00:00:56,094 --> 00:00:58,763
<i>"What makes a Great Teacher?"</i>

19
00:00:58,830 --> 00:01:01,499
<i>To answer the homework you gave me…</i>

20
00:01:01,566 --> 00:01:04,035
-It's fun!
-It's very, very interesting!

21
00:01:04,102 --> 00:01:05,970
-Why not join us?
-How about it?

22
00:01:06,037 --> 00:01:07,705
Our Drill Team is recruiting!

23
00:01:07,772 --> 00:01:11,242
<i>It must be a teacher who never gives up</i>

24
00:01:11,309 --> 00:01:15,480
<i>until the very end, and who thinks</i>
<i>about what is best for the students.</i>

25
00:01:15,547 --> 00:01:17,949
<i>I think that is the answer.</i>

26
00:01:18,850 --> 00:01:20,919
I think this should work.

27
00:01:22,854 --> 00:01:28,092
WHAT AN OBVIOUS ANSWER
DON'T SAY IT SO PROUDLY

28
00:01:33,398 --> 00:01:34,365
Good morning.

29
00:01:36,334 --> 00:01:37,902
Good morning.

30
00:01:37,969 --> 00:01:40,138
Good morning.

31
00:01:40,205 --> 00:01:41,172
Hmm?

32
00:01:41,973 --> 00:01:43,741
Wait a minute, just now,

33
00:01:43,808 --> 00:01:46,678
you responded to
Ms. Kashiwabara's "good morning,"

34
00:01:46,744 --> 00:01:48,680
but ignored my "good morning," right?

35
00:01:48,746 --> 00:01:50,748
That's not true.

36
00:01:50,815 --> 00:01:51,649
Right?

37
00:01:51,716 --> 00:01:53,017
You're just imagining it.

38
00:01:53,084 --> 00:01:56,454
Well, if you say so.
All 28 of you are here today,

39
00:01:56,521 --> 00:02:00,091
so if you ever have any problems like
Ken-Ken and Yuukichi did, tell me.

40
00:02:00,158 --> 00:02:02,827
If there's anything I can do,
I'll do whatever it takes.

41
00:02:02,894 --> 00:02:05,964
Heck, you can even call me
"Great Teacher" if you want.

42
00:02:07,966 --> 00:02:08,900
Mr. Onizuka.

43
00:02:08,967 --> 00:02:09,801
What is it?

44
00:02:10,501 --> 00:02:14,639
Maybe Ms. Kashiwabara also
has some passionate words to share?

45
00:02:14,706 --> 00:02:17,508
No. I just thought
I should hand these out.

46
00:02:18,443 --> 00:02:19,577
Please go ahead.

47
00:02:21,079 --> 00:02:22,714
My next class

48
00:02:22,780 --> 00:02:25,817
will have you work in pairs,
so please check them.

49
00:02:29,354 --> 00:02:31,556
I'm with you, Yuukichi?

50
00:02:32,090 --> 00:02:34,225
Hey! That's my line.

51
00:02:34,292 --> 00:02:35,460
Ms. Ishibashi.

52
00:02:36,027 --> 00:02:37,228
Nice to work with you.

53
00:02:38,129 --> 00:02:39,964
Yeah. Likewise.

54
00:02:40,632 --> 00:02:42,600
I took your wishes into consideration,

55
00:02:42,667 --> 00:02:45,503
so it should be fine,
but if there's any issue, do tell me.

56
00:02:45,570 --> 00:02:47,071
Okay, thanks.

57
00:02:47,138 --> 00:02:49,040
I'm kind of jealous.

58
00:02:49,107 --> 00:02:51,776
When I was in high school,
we didn't have classes

59
00:02:51,843 --> 00:02:54,312
where students joined forces
and gave it their all.

60
00:02:54,379 --> 00:02:56,247
It's nothing so frivolous.

61
00:02:56,314 --> 00:03:00,885
The purpose is to cultivate communication
skills among students, right?

62
00:03:00,952 --> 00:03:02,287
Ms. Kashiwabara.

63
00:03:02,353 --> 00:03:03,254
That's right.

64
00:03:03,321 --> 00:03:05,590
Pair-work also fosters cooperativeness

65
00:03:05,657 --> 00:03:07,992
and encourages
an independent learning attitude.

66
00:03:08,626 --> 00:03:09,494
That's right.

67
00:03:11,329 --> 00:03:14,198
You all haven't looked me
in the eyes today,

68
00:03:14,265 --> 00:03:17,035
and I get the sense I'm being ignored.

69
00:03:17,101 --> 00:03:18,403
You're just imagining it.

70
00:03:19,237 --> 00:03:20,772
We aren't doing that at all.

71
00:03:34,952 --> 00:03:37,221
They were definitely ignoring me,
those kids!

72
00:03:37,288 --> 00:03:38,289
Onicchi, wait!

73
00:03:38,356 --> 00:03:40,191
What? Huh?

74
00:03:41,359 --> 00:03:42,226
Huh?

75
00:03:43,995 --> 00:03:45,330
Thanks, the both of you.

76
00:03:45,396 --> 00:03:46,297
For what?

77
00:03:46,364 --> 00:03:49,467
You two were the only ones
to look me in the eyes.

78
00:03:50,435 --> 00:03:51,936
This is about that.

79
00:03:53,705 --> 00:03:56,007
The other day, we got this post.

80
00:03:56,074 --> 00:03:58,076
LET'S ACT LIKE ONIZUKA DOESN'T EXIST

81
00:03:58,142 --> 00:03:59,877
Who would do such a thing?

82
00:03:59,944 --> 00:04:00,778
Who knows.

83
00:04:01,946 --> 00:04:02,780
Could it be…

84
00:04:03,448 --> 00:04:07,452
It's like this class has
a hidden mastermind, like on TV…

85
00:04:07,952 --> 00:04:10,054
-No, that's a bit…
-I don't think so.

86
00:04:10,121 --> 00:04:11,856
There's no bullying or anything.

87
00:04:12,357 --> 00:04:16,794
If anything, they all just don't want
their own world to be disturbed.

88
00:04:16,861 --> 00:04:17,795
Yeah, exactly.

89
00:04:17,862 --> 00:04:22,200
Then, why does everyone act
in perfect unison when they see this?

90
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:26,804
"Let's act like Onizuka doesn't exist."

91
00:04:26,871 --> 00:04:28,573
Well, you see…

92
00:04:28,639 --> 00:04:31,008
It's kind of persuasive.

93
00:04:31,075 --> 00:04:35,480
Ever since our previous homeroom teacher,
someone has been making these posts.

94
00:04:36,214 --> 00:04:37,448
In this case, when we thought,

95
00:04:37,515 --> 00:04:41,719
"Onicchi is barging in here,
bossing us around, he's annoying,"

96
00:04:41,786 --> 00:04:44,422
they made a perfectly timed comment.

97
00:04:44,489 --> 00:04:45,423
Yeah, exactly.

98
00:06:14,479 --> 00:06:19,550
It's like how, with social media,
malicious posts can spread like wildfire.

99
00:06:20,184 --> 00:06:24,922
Those who post things like this
enjoy seeing people influenced by them.

100
00:06:25,857 --> 00:06:27,959
Then, what do you think I should do?

101
00:06:28,025 --> 00:06:30,228
Just do what you want, Mr. Onizuka.

102
00:06:30,294 --> 00:06:32,930
There you go saying that again!

103
00:06:32,997 --> 00:06:34,198
Miss, do you have a moment?

104
00:06:34,265 --> 00:06:35,566
What's wrong? Kotone.

105
00:06:35,633 --> 00:06:37,368
I need to talk to you, Ms. Kashiwabara.

106
00:06:37,435 --> 00:06:40,571
Tell me instead.
I'll listen to anything you have to say.

107
00:06:40,638 --> 00:06:41,806
I'm sorry.

108
00:06:41,873 --> 00:06:44,909
It's a delicate matter,
I can't tell a tactless man like you.

109
00:06:44,976 --> 00:06:46,010
Okay.

110
00:06:49,680 --> 00:06:50,715
Ms. Koizumi.

111
00:06:50,781 --> 00:06:53,651
What do you think
this "delicate matter" is?

112
00:06:53,718 --> 00:06:57,221
Who knows. It may be an issue
that she can only tell a woman.

113
00:06:57,288 --> 00:06:59,323
It's so troublesome, isn't it?

114
00:06:59,390 --> 00:07:01,626
Male teachers can't say anything careless.

115
00:07:01,692 --> 00:07:06,697
Lately, even when I talk to my wife
and daughter, I worry about compliance.

116
00:07:06,764 --> 00:07:07,832
No.

117
00:07:07,899 --> 00:07:10,201
If you have something to say,
just say it clearly.

118
00:07:10,268 --> 00:07:12,203
Like, "Goodbye, compliance."

119
00:07:12,270 --> 00:07:13,738
You can't do that!

120
00:07:13,804 --> 00:07:15,606
Don't just pop up out of nowhere!

121
00:07:15,673 --> 00:07:18,509
In this era, that sort of thing
doesn't fly anymore.

122
00:07:18,576 --> 00:07:22,113
Stop acting like
the old days were so great

123
00:07:22,179 --> 00:07:24,815
and update yourself
to fit the times already.

124
00:07:24,882 --> 00:07:27,785
If we have love
and conviction on our side…

125
00:07:27,852 --> 00:07:29,487
Those things are invisible

126
00:07:29,554 --> 00:07:33,291
and can't be proven, so the students
and parents won't understand.

127
00:07:33,858 --> 00:07:38,729
Besides, when someone like you
breaks the rules and causes problems,

128
00:07:38,796 --> 00:07:40,665
it troubles the other teachers too.

129
00:07:41,365 --> 00:07:42,300
Is that so?

130
00:07:45,636 --> 00:07:49,240
My mission as the vice-principal

131
00:07:49,307 --> 00:07:51,742
is to make sure
all the teachers at our school

132
00:07:51,809 --> 00:07:55,012
can do their jobs a little bit easier.

133
00:07:55,980 --> 00:07:56,948
For that purpose,

134
00:07:57,014 --> 00:08:00,785
I am prepared to become a shield
to protect the children here,

135
00:08:00,851 --> 00:08:05,389
and I'm sure all of you
understand my efforts.

136
00:08:05,456 --> 00:08:07,658
Is that the case?

137
00:08:13,764 --> 00:08:16,067
What did Kotone say?

138
00:08:16,133 --> 00:08:18,135
Seems she wants to change her partner.

139
00:08:18,202 --> 00:08:19,036
What?

140
00:08:19,103 --> 00:08:19,937
Oh…

141
00:08:20,972 --> 00:08:24,041
Her partner is Ayumu Yoshida?

142
00:08:25,042 --> 00:08:27,745
What exactly doesn't she like about him?

143
00:08:27,812 --> 00:08:29,046
Apparently,

144
00:08:29,981 --> 00:08:33,084
he's been glaring at her lately,
and it's creeping her out.

145
00:08:52,803 --> 00:08:54,605
Mr. Ayumu?

146
00:08:55,673 --> 00:08:58,142
Do you have a moment?

147
00:08:58,843 --> 00:08:59,910
What is it?

148
00:08:59,977 --> 00:09:00,945
It's just…

149
00:09:01,846 --> 00:09:06,150
Kotone said she feels
like you're always glaring at her.

150
00:09:06,717 --> 00:09:08,552
What? What's that about?
I'm not doing that.

151
00:09:08,619 --> 00:09:10,554
Maybe she's scared of that look.

152
00:09:11,122 --> 00:09:12,523
Though I'm sure you're being serious.

153
00:09:13,224 --> 00:09:14,158
Serious?

154
00:09:15,760 --> 00:09:17,695
You like Kotone, don't you?

155
00:09:20,131 --> 00:09:23,534
I don't want you to misunderstand,
it's not like I care about her.

156
00:09:24,535 --> 00:09:26,804
She just happens to be
in my line of sight.

157
00:09:27,405 --> 00:09:30,307
Okay! Then I'll go tell her that.

158
00:09:31,575 --> 00:09:34,412
"He doesn't have feelings for you.
Don't be stupid and misunderstand…"

159
00:09:34,478 --> 00:09:35,513
Hey!

160
00:09:35,579 --> 00:09:36,647
"Hey"?

161
00:09:36,714 --> 00:09:37,548
What is it?

162
00:09:38,683 --> 00:09:40,418
No, but…

163
00:09:41,052 --> 00:09:43,054
You do like her, right?

164
00:09:45,089 --> 00:09:48,059
Then, why don't you just tell her?

165
00:09:48,592 --> 00:09:50,661
There's no way it'll go smoothly.

166
00:09:50,728 --> 00:09:51,862
Why?

167
00:09:51,929 --> 00:09:54,632
Because I have nothing going for me.

168
00:09:58,769 --> 00:10:00,838
I'm not cool like Soma.

169
00:10:03,874 --> 00:10:05,976
I'm not smart like Itsuki.

170
00:10:07,111 --> 00:10:10,648
I'm bad at sports too,
so I'm envious of Hiroto.

171
00:10:10,715 --> 00:10:13,884
What are you saying? I'm sure
you have plenty of good qualities.

172
00:10:14,552 --> 00:10:15,519
For example?

173
00:10:16,454 --> 00:10:17,288
Well…

174
00:10:17,855 --> 00:10:20,157
That would be…

175
00:10:21,992 --> 00:10:24,161
You eat your food
without leaving leftovers,

176
00:10:24,962 --> 00:10:26,864
and you do the cleaning properly.

177
00:10:26,931 --> 00:10:28,999
You're never late, either.

178
00:10:29,066 --> 00:10:30,134
Anyone can do that.

179
00:10:30,201 --> 00:10:34,105
No, don't give up, keep trying.
I'll help you with anything.

180
00:10:35,506 --> 00:10:38,275
Then, can you make Kotone like me?

181
00:10:38,342 --> 00:10:40,611
Hang on, how would I do that?

182
00:10:40,678 --> 00:10:43,414
Think about that yourself.
There must be plenty of ways.

183
00:10:43,481 --> 00:10:47,218
Like subtly making her think, "Good things
will happen if I go out with him."

184
00:10:47,284 --> 00:10:49,920
But don't tell her I like her.
I don't want to be hated.

185
00:10:49,987 --> 00:10:53,090
What a difficult request…

186
00:10:56,827 --> 00:10:58,062
There she is.

187
00:11:01,632 --> 00:11:02,967
This book, please.

188
00:11:03,033 --> 00:11:04,101
9 - LITERATURE

189
00:11:06,470 --> 00:11:08,405
Ms. Kotone Wakatsuki.

190
00:11:08,472 --> 00:11:11,342
Please return the book by this date.

191
00:11:11,408 --> 00:11:12,243
Okay.

192
00:11:13,410 --> 00:11:15,112
Thank you very much.

193
00:11:26,123 --> 00:11:29,260
Ms. Kotone, do you have a moment?

194
00:11:29,326 --> 00:11:31,929
It's about Ayumu.

195
00:11:31,996 --> 00:11:33,330
What about him?

196
00:11:34,064 --> 00:11:36,801
He isn't glaring at you.

197
00:11:36,867 --> 00:11:40,304
It's just that when he gets serious,
his face looks like that.

198
00:11:40,971 --> 00:11:42,339
Serious?

199
00:11:42,406 --> 00:11:45,509
No, it's… Well, you know…

200
00:11:47,111 --> 00:11:50,881
I think he might like you.

201
00:11:51,682 --> 00:11:52,516
What?

202
00:11:53,083 --> 00:11:55,686
Why don't you try going out with him?

203
00:11:55,753 --> 00:11:58,923
He may look like that, but you can feel
he hides a burning passion.

204
00:11:58,989 --> 00:12:01,458
They say you can't judge
a book by its cover, no?

205
00:12:01,525 --> 00:12:03,060
I just said something
pretty good, didn't I?

206
00:12:03,627 --> 00:12:05,229
Please be quiet.

207
00:12:05,930 --> 00:12:07,064
Oh, sorry.

208
00:12:07,865 --> 00:12:11,202
-Excuse me.
-Wait a minute! Hold up!

209
00:12:11,268 --> 00:12:15,673
Please tell him
I have no intention of dating anyone.

210
00:12:19,476 --> 00:12:20,411
Kotone.

211
00:12:20,477 --> 00:12:24,515
I mean romance is not worth it at all,
and it's troublesome!

212
00:12:25,282 --> 00:12:27,451
Getting anxious when a text
doesn't get a reply…

213
00:12:27,518 --> 00:12:30,421
Or getting jealous when the person
you like talks to someone else…

214
00:12:30,487 --> 00:12:34,491
If I'm going to waste energy like that,
reading a book is way better.

215
00:12:35,125 --> 00:12:36,694
When you put it like that…

216
00:12:39,897 --> 00:12:42,666
So, did you tell Ayumu Yoshida?

217
00:12:42,733 --> 00:12:46,303
Well, I couldn't just lie to him.

218
00:12:46,370 --> 00:12:47,204
And then?

219
00:12:49,673 --> 00:12:50,507
I'm done for.

220
00:12:51,609 --> 00:12:55,246
Hey, don't give up so easily.

221
00:12:55,312 --> 00:12:56,146
What?

222
00:12:56,213 --> 00:12:58,549
What are you talking about?
It's your fault.

223
00:12:58,616 --> 00:13:00,584
Why did you go and say that I like her?

224
00:13:01,185 --> 00:13:07,057
I only said that you might like her.

225
00:13:07,124 --> 00:13:08,158
Enough already.

226
00:13:08,225 --> 00:13:09,727
Please tell her

227
00:13:09,793 --> 00:13:12,963
she won't have to see me again
until graduation, so rest easy.

228
00:13:13,030 --> 00:13:14,531
Ayumu.

229
00:13:15,032 --> 00:13:17,368
Does this mean he's finally over it?

230
00:13:17,434 --> 00:13:18,402
No.

231
00:13:18,469 --> 00:13:20,738
Leaving it like this
just leaves a bad taste.

232
00:13:20,804 --> 00:13:24,808
If he's going to get rejected, I think
it's best he expresses his feelings first.

233
00:13:24,875 --> 00:13:28,112
And Kotone shouldn't just say
she doesn't want to date anyone.

234
00:13:28,679 --> 00:13:30,648
I can understand her feelings, though.

235
00:13:31,548 --> 00:13:32,383
What?

236
00:13:32,449 --> 00:13:33,284
Huh?

237
00:13:34,952 --> 00:13:36,120
Why is that?

238
00:13:36,186 --> 00:13:38,989
I also find romance to be a hassle,

239
00:13:39,056 --> 00:13:41,358
so if I ever want to date,
I'll just use an app.

240
00:13:41,425 --> 00:13:44,795
What? Isn't that dangerous?
Those are dating sites, right?

241
00:13:44,862 --> 00:13:48,465
It's very like you
to have those prejudices,

242
00:13:48,532 --> 00:13:51,669
but even the government
promotes those apps nowadays.

243
00:13:51,735 --> 00:13:53,938
You can see the users'
hobbies and interests,

244
00:13:54,004 --> 00:13:56,206
so you can easily choose your type.

245
00:13:56,273 --> 00:14:01,812
No, but leaving human relationships,
the most important thing to us,

246
00:14:01,879 --> 00:14:04,181
up to an AI to decide,
isn't that a bit off?

247
00:14:04,248 --> 00:14:05,616
Right, Ms. Koizumi?

248
00:14:06,583 --> 00:14:09,753
I married a man I chose myself.

249
00:14:09,820 --> 00:14:11,655
And I bitterly regret it.

250
00:14:12,356 --> 00:14:15,125
Once my child grows up,
I plan to use an app.

251
00:14:15,192 --> 00:14:17,728
Huh? Ms. Koizumi, are you a single mother?

252
00:14:17,795 --> 00:14:19,463
Is there a problem?

253
00:14:19,530 --> 00:14:20,931
Of course not.

254
00:14:22,633 --> 00:14:24,201
What about you, Mr. Abe?

255
00:14:24,268 --> 00:14:27,004
I have no interest in marriage
in the first place.

256
00:14:27,071 --> 00:14:28,038
What?

257
00:14:28,105 --> 00:14:31,375
Mr. Abe, have you never
dated anyone before?

258
00:14:32,576 --> 00:14:34,311
Is it necessary to answer that?

259
00:14:34,378 --> 00:14:35,612
Not at all.

260
00:14:37,881 --> 00:14:38,749
Hey.

261
00:14:39,750 --> 00:14:43,520
Mr. Murayama, I'm sure
you don't know much about those "apps"?

262
00:14:44,688 --> 00:14:46,357
My wife and daughter tell me…

263
00:14:46,423 --> 00:14:49,526
"If you divorce,
there are apps for seniors.

264
00:14:49,593 --> 00:14:51,061
You can find a partner there."

265
00:14:51,128 --> 00:14:53,063
Mr. Murayama, are you getting divorced?

266
00:14:53,130 --> 00:14:54,932
No, it's just a joke.

267
00:14:54,999 --> 00:14:57,101
What about you, Mr. Onizuka?

268
00:14:57,167 --> 00:14:58,302
For me…

269
00:14:58,369 --> 00:15:00,137
It was like a spark when we met.

270
00:15:00,204 --> 00:15:02,840
We're bound by destiny,
so even now we're lovey-dovey.

271
00:15:02,906 --> 00:15:04,208
Mr. Onizuka!

272
00:15:04,274 --> 00:15:08,412
Your wife sent me an email,
for old times' sake.

273
00:15:08,479 --> 00:15:09,380
What?

274
00:15:09,446 --> 00:15:12,383
It's heartwarming. You don't mind
if I let everyone hear it, right?

275
00:15:12,950 --> 00:15:14,218
Hey.

276
00:15:14,284 --> 00:15:15,919
"Mr. Nakamaru,

277
00:15:15,986 --> 00:15:19,223
is my husband doing his job properly?

278
00:15:19,289 --> 00:15:23,127
If he is causing trouble like he used to,

279
00:15:23,193 --> 00:15:26,130
please feel free to give him an earful.

280
00:15:26,196 --> 00:15:29,566
He has been getting quite cocky lately."

281
00:15:29,633 --> 00:15:33,370
Wow, what a lovely wife you have!

282
00:15:33,437 --> 00:15:35,539
Why did she marry a man like you?

283
00:15:35,606 --> 00:15:38,308
I bet your wife loves you lots, huh?

284
00:15:38,375 --> 00:15:39,910
-Oh!
-What?

285
00:15:40,744 --> 00:15:42,613
It's best not to say that.

286
00:15:42,679 --> 00:15:43,514
What?

287
00:15:45,182 --> 00:15:49,319
His wife just divorced him last year.

288
00:15:49,386 --> 00:15:50,554
His second divorce.

289
00:15:50,621 --> 00:15:51,622
What, no way!

290
00:16:00,931 --> 00:16:03,233
What about you, Principal?

291
00:16:03,300 --> 00:16:04,835
I've been married three times,

292
00:16:04,902 --> 00:16:08,305
so even now child support
and alimony are a struggle for me.

293
00:16:09,306 --> 00:16:10,474
Sounds tough.

294
00:16:30,561 --> 00:16:32,996
I wasn't looking at her.

295
00:16:34,865 --> 00:16:36,166
Don't push yourself.

296
00:16:36,733 --> 00:16:38,168
I'm not.

297
00:16:39,002 --> 00:16:41,805
I don't care about her anymore anyway.

298
00:16:41,872 --> 00:16:42,706
Hey.

299
00:16:43,474 --> 00:16:45,843
Can I ask you one thing?

300
00:16:46,710 --> 00:16:47,678
What?

301
00:16:50,614 --> 00:16:52,716
What do you like about Kotone?

302
00:16:53,884 --> 00:16:54,785
What?

303
00:16:54,852 --> 00:16:58,088
She's always reading a book.

304
00:16:58,889 --> 00:16:59,990
It's nice, huh?

305
00:17:01,191 --> 00:17:02,593
There's that too, but…

306
00:17:03,560 --> 00:17:04,394
But?

307
00:17:05,496 --> 00:17:08,532
We ran into each other
at the shopping district once before.

308
00:17:09,366 --> 00:17:12,503
<i>Even though she was meeting</i>
<i>my mother for the first time…</i>

309
00:17:12,569 --> 00:17:13,937
Nice to meet you.

310
00:17:14,004 --> 00:17:16,340
<i>I was so shocked, I couldn't say anything.</i>

311
00:17:16,406 --> 00:17:19,109
<i>I thought, "Wow, she's really mature."</i>

312
00:17:19,776 --> 00:17:23,413
Even the store clerks and the librarian,

313
00:17:23,480 --> 00:17:25,682
she never fails to greet them.

314
00:17:25,749 --> 00:17:30,420
I don't think there are many people
our age who can do that.

315
00:17:34,591 --> 00:17:35,559
What?

316
00:17:36,493 --> 00:17:39,496
Those feelings of yours…

317
00:17:39,563 --> 00:17:41,131
You should share them.

318
00:17:41,865 --> 00:17:42,699
What?

319
00:17:43,333 --> 00:17:44,868
Kotone will surely be happy.

320
00:17:45,502 --> 00:17:47,804
If she knows
that you think of her that way.

321
00:17:48,605 --> 00:17:49,706
Do you think so?

322
00:17:56,547 --> 00:18:00,083
All right. Operation Confession is a go!

323
00:18:00,584 --> 00:18:01,418
What?

324
00:18:01,485 --> 00:18:03,387
What's with that lame name?

325
00:18:03,887 --> 00:18:09,259
Before we start the strategy meeting,
let me introduce today's special lecturer.

326
00:18:09,326 --> 00:18:10,661
What?

327
00:18:10,727 --> 00:18:12,262
Mr. Ryunosuke Miyazawa.

328
00:18:13,830 --> 00:18:14,665
Hello.

329
00:18:15,699 --> 00:18:18,268
I feel like I've seen him before.
But who is he?

330
00:18:18,335 --> 00:18:21,538
He's someone dispatched
from the company that runs our school.

331
00:18:22,506 --> 00:18:23,507
Ryunosuke.

332
00:18:24,441 --> 00:18:27,644
By the way, he's a former student of mine.

333
00:18:27,711 --> 00:18:28,579
Really?

334
00:18:28,645 --> 00:18:31,515
No way! And he still grew up
to be a proper adult?

335
00:18:31,582 --> 00:18:32,983
Shut up.

336
00:18:33,050 --> 00:18:34,818
But why is he here?

337
00:18:34,885 --> 00:18:39,156
Ryunosuke has made
countless women cry in the past.

338
00:18:39,223 --> 00:18:42,159
If you listen to his advice,
success is guaranteed!

339
00:18:42,226 --> 00:18:44,494
Please don't spread
misinformation, Mr. Onizuka.

340
00:18:45,529 --> 00:18:47,798
Well then, any strategies?

341
00:18:48,398 --> 00:18:50,934
Maybe a bike ride to the sea?

342
00:18:51,001 --> 00:18:53,704
Or maybe we change your hairstyle?

343
00:18:53,770 --> 00:18:57,908
Or a present? Maybe even a ring?

344
00:19:00,844 --> 00:19:04,248
I figured that's how
you flirted with women…

345
00:19:04,314 --> 00:19:06,583
Bet you failed every single time.

346
00:19:06,650 --> 00:19:10,287
Shut up.
Then how did you do it, Ryunosuke?

347
00:19:10,354 --> 00:19:12,289
I've never confessed to anyone myself.

348
00:19:12,356 --> 00:19:13,957
Damn! You make me mad.

349
00:19:14,024 --> 00:19:17,427
Master, please teach me how to be popular.

350
00:19:17,494 --> 00:19:19,429
Hey, this isn't about you.

351
00:19:21,798 --> 00:19:24,735
Yeah, right now it's about Ayumu.

352
00:19:24,801 --> 00:19:26,303
We have to think of something.

353
00:19:27,237 --> 00:19:31,174
If I recall, she said
his face was scary, right?

354
00:19:32,242 --> 00:19:34,878
So for now, you need to look
more cheerful.

355
00:19:34,945 --> 00:19:37,347
Maybe show that you have
a playful side too?

356
00:19:37,414 --> 00:19:38,282
How?

357
00:19:38,348 --> 00:19:40,884
Let's see, for example…

358
00:19:40,951 --> 00:19:42,352
Uh…

359
00:19:42,919 --> 00:19:44,254
What about DAIGO-speak?

360
00:19:44,321 --> 00:19:45,889
Oh, that might be pretty good.

361
00:19:45,956 --> 00:19:47,391
What's that?

362
00:19:47,457 --> 00:19:49,026
You don't know about it?

363
00:19:49,092 --> 00:19:51,762
Those acronyms that DAIGO,
the celebrity, often uses.

364
00:19:54,064 --> 00:19:57,267
I think I saw him in a video.
He abbreviates things, right?

365
00:19:57,834 --> 00:20:01,204
For example, KDO.

366
00:20:01,271 --> 00:20:04,408
"Kotone Do you want to go Out?"

367
00:20:04,474 --> 00:20:06,643
It's easier than saying it as is, right?

368
00:20:07,210 --> 00:20:08,478
I see!

369
00:20:16,386 --> 00:20:17,454
He's coming back.

370
00:20:18,088 --> 00:20:19,756
How did it go?

371
00:20:20,757 --> 00:20:22,359
I thought about it a lot,

372
00:20:22,993 --> 00:20:25,162
and I said KAU.

373
00:20:26,430 --> 00:20:28,098
KAU?

374
00:20:28,932 --> 00:20:31,168
"Kotone, Are you Up for hanging out?"

375
00:20:32,336 --> 00:20:33,970
Oh, that's good!

376
00:20:34,037 --> 00:20:35,372
How did she respond?

377
00:20:35,939 --> 00:20:37,040
GM.

378
00:20:37,107 --> 00:20:38,275
What?

379
00:20:38,342 --> 00:20:40,344
GM? Oh!

380
00:20:43,380 --> 00:20:45,515
"Get away from Me."

381
00:20:51,655 --> 00:20:54,825
I knew it, a love letter is the way to go!

382
00:20:55,425 --> 00:20:57,694
But what should I write?

383
00:20:58,562 --> 00:21:01,965
When I want to keep a conversation
going over messaging or text,

384
00:21:02,032 --> 00:21:05,235
I try to ask questions that grab
the other person's interest.

385
00:21:05,302 --> 00:21:06,937
For example?

386
00:21:07,003 --> 00:21:08,572
One I often use is,

387
00:21:08,638 --> 00:21:10,340
"If a genie in a lamp

388
00:21:10,407 --> 00:21:14,044
granted you three wishes,
what would you wish for?"

389
00:21:14,111 --> 00:21:15,112
I don't have any.

390
00:21:15,645 --> 00:21:16,780
What?

391
00:21:16,847 --> 00:21:20,951
Genies don't exist, and if you have
a wish, you have to work to realize it.

392
00:21:22,319 --> 00:21:24,688
I see, you're absolutely right.

393
00:21:24,755 --> 00:21:26,356
But right now, I might have one.

394
00:21:26,423 --> 00:21:27,724
Oh, what is it?

395
00:21:29,226 --> 00:21:31,395
For you to stop interrupting my reading.

396
00:21:32,329 --> 00:21:33,363
Bye!

397
00:21:33,430 --> 00:21:34,464
Bye.

398
00:21:36,500 --> 00:21:39,669
STRATEGY MEETING 3

399
00:21:39,736 --> 00:21:41,738
What are we going to do now, Ryunosuke?

400
00:21:41,805 --> 00:21:43,206
Huh? Oh, right.

401
00:21:43,273 --> 00:21:45,509
Are you actually popular with girls?

402
00:21:45,575 --> 00:21:48,512
Listen, I've never
had to confess to anyone!

403
00:21:48,578 --> 00:21:49,446
Oh!

404
00:21:50,080 --> 00:21:53,283
If Kotone likes books,
there's always that move.

405
00:21:53,350 --> 00:21:54,718
The one you see on TV.

406
00:21:54,785 --> 00:21:56,987
I don't watch TV shows. What do you mean?

407
00:21:57,053 --> 00:21:57,988
Like,

408
00:21:58,922 --> 00:22:03,427
as a girl reaches out to take a book,
someone else's hand touches hers.

409
00:22:03,994 --> 00:22:06,296
In that moment, for some reason,

410
00:22:06,863 --> 00:22:08,398
her heart skips a beat.

411
00:22:09,599 --> 00:22:10,634
<i>When she looks,</i>

412
00:22:10,700 --> 00:22:13,670
<i>there is a wonderful guy</i>
<i>reaching for the same book,</i>

413
00:22:13,737 --> 00:22:16,440
<i>"Do you like this novel?"</i>

414
00:22:16,506 --> 00:22:21,645
<i>"I like it too," and like that,</i>
<i>the two of them instantly fall in love.</i>

415
00:22:24,648 --> 00:22:25,649
What are you doing?

416
00:22:50,340 --> 00:22:52,175
What a coincidence.

417
00:22:53,477 --> 00:22:54,778
Do you like this book?

418
00:22:56,012 --> 00:22:57,214
So do I.

419
00:22:57,280 --> 00:22:59,249
<i>Cyrano de Bergerac </i>is great, isn't it?

420
00:22:59,316 --> 00:23:02,352
The main character's feelings
really tug at your heartstrings.

421
00:23:02,419 --> 00:23:04,287
You can really empathize with him.

422
00:23:04,354 --> 00:23:09,092
The fact that you chose this book,
could it be destiny?

423
00:23:09,159 --> 00:23:09,993
So,

424
00:23:11,928 --> 00:23:15,665
if you'd like, next time,
would you… with me?

425
00:23:21,805 --> 00:23:23,273
Excuse me!

426
00:23:35,051 --> 00:23:35,719
CLASS 1-B

427
00:23:35,785 --> 00:23:37,554
Why did you run away?

428
00:23:37,621 --> 00:23:38,989
I mean…

429
00:23:39,055 --> 00:23:41,892
The more I talked,
the more put off by me she seemed.

430
00:23:42,792 --> 00:23:47,163
Also, why are you so polite around Kotone?

431
00:23:47,230 --> 00:23:51,167
You can't blame me,
we're classmates but we've barely spoken.

432
00:23:51,735 --> 00:23:53,770
Don't say such pathetic things.

433
00:23:53,837 --> 00:23:55,939
Act more like a man!

434
00:23:57,507 --> 00:23:58,642
Women…

435
00:23:59,309 --> 00:24:01,778
They prefer a guy who makes them think,

436
00:24:02,279 --> 00:24:05,549
"What's up with him? He's the worst.
But I'm curious, my heart is pounding."

437
00:24:05,615 --> 00:24:08,051
Rather than a guy who is just "nice."

438
00:24:08,118 --> 00:24:11,254
-Is that how it is, Master?
-I think it depends on the person.

439
00:24:11,821 --> 00:24:14,024
I'm just going to give up.

440
00:24:14,090 --> 00:24:16,059
Don't say that.

441
00:24:16,693 --> 00:24:20,030
Ms. Kashiwabara,
do you have any good ideas?

442
00:24:20,096 --> 00:24:23,266
Personally, I think you'd be
better off consulting an AI.

443
00:24:24,334 --> 00:24:25,669
Right, that's an option.

444
00:24:25,735 --> 00:24:28,805
No, you've worked so hard to get this far.

445
00:24:28,872 --> 00:24:31,207
Ayumu, now that it's come to this,

446
00:24:31,875 --> 00:24:34,244
you just have to share
your feelings with her directly.

447
00:24:34,878 --> 00:24:38,949
Right, don't you have
a dream or something?

448
00:24:39,015 --> 00:24:39,783
What?

449
00:24:41,451 --> 00:24:43,753
Since ancient times, men have always

450
00:24:43,820 --> 00:24:46,489
talked about their dreams
to the women they love.

451
00:24:46,556 --> 00:24:48,224
What? Is that true?

452
00:24:48,291 --> 00:24:50,460
I've never done that myself.

453
00:24:51,027 --> 00:24:52,028
Ayumu.

454
00:24:52,729 --> 00:24:54,798
Don't you have a dream?

455
00:24:56,366 --> 00:24:58,234
It's not that I don't have one, but…

456
00:24:58,301 --> 00:25:01,738
Oh, I got it. A lawyer or a doctor.

457
00:25:02,739 --> 00:25:04,774
You like listening to music, maybe a band?

458
00:25:05,442 --> 00:25:08,878
Nowadays, kids also want to be
a pro gamer or a YouTuber!

459
00:25:10,046 --> 00:25:13,450
I never had the courage
to tell anyone before.

460
00:25:16,353 --> 00:25:17,354
You won't laugh, right?

461
00:25:17,921 --> 00:25:19,122
No way I would.

462
00:25:19,723 --> 00:25:20,624
Right?

463
00:25:23,827 --> 00:25:25,528
The UN Secretary-General.

464
00:25:30,266 --> 00:25:31,134
Wait, why?

465
00:25:31,768 --> 00:25:33,103
I want to protect the Earth.

466
00:25:36,439 --> 00:25:38,008
Sorry, what do you mean?

467
00:25:38,074 --> 00:25:41,144
I mean, I want to reform the current UN,

468
00:25:41,211 --> 00:25:44,347
abolish the permanent membership system,
eliminate war from the world,

469
00:25:44,414 --> 00:25:48,385
and make countries all over the world
fight hard against global warming.

470
00:25:48,451 --> 00:25:51,988
Otherwise, if things stay the way
they are, humanity will go extinct.

471
00:25:57,994 --> 00:26:00,463
I knew it. You think it's dumb.

472
00:26:04,734 --> 00:26:05,802
You're pretty

473
00:26:07,070 --> 00:26:08,338
amazing.

474
00:26:09,406 --> 00:26:10,240
What?

475
00:26:10,807 --> 00:26:12,809
When I was a high school freshman,

476
00:26:12,876 --> 00:26:16,680
I never thought about
anything so high-level,

477
00:26:16,746 --> 00:26:19,482
so I think this is
something special about you!

478
00:26:19,549 --> 00:26:20,650
Right, Ms. Kashiwabara?

479
00:26:21,384 --> 00:26:24,120
Galileo was also mocked
by those around him at first,

480
00:26:24,187 --> 00:26:27,757
but he stuck to his convictions and made
a huge contribution to humanity.

481
00:26:27,824 --> 00:26:33,430
When I first met my wife,
she didn't see me as an option,

482
00:26:33,496 --> 00:26:37,901
but I didn't give up and swore to love
only her, and we got married.

483
00:26:37,967 --> 00:26:40,603
But she's left you right now, right?

484
00:26:40,670 --> 00:26:45,575
Well, on TV, heroes have
to go through… a crisis, right?

485
00:26:46,409 --> 00:26:48,311
Anyway, never mind about me.

486
00:26:51,314 --> 00:26:52,182
Ayumu.

487
00:26:54,918 --> 00:26:57,053
The only thing you need…

488
00:26:59,489 --> 00:27:00,657
is courage.

489
00:27:07,497 --> 00:27:09,566
That's her room.

490
00:27:09,632 --> 00:27:12,235
Hey, how do you even know that?

491
00:27:12,302 --> 00:27:15,438
When going home, I often
take the long way to pass by here.

492
00:27:15,505 --> 00:27:17,540
Wait, that's just stalking.

493
00:27:17,607 --> 00:27:18,842
Don't say that right now.

494
00:27:18,908 --> 00:27:20,443
All right, everyone.

495
00:27:20,510 --> 00:27:23,713
Stand by… start! Here we go!

496
00:27:26,282 --> 00:27:28,151
-Hurry up!
-Hey, what are you doing?

497
00:27:28,218 --> 00:27:29,519
Making it rain, what else?

498
00:27:29,586 --> 00:27:30,920
Why?

499
00:27:30,987 --> 00:27:32,689
It makes things more exciting!

500
00:27:33,423 --> 00:27:35,658
When Kotone sees you drenched to the bone,

501
00:27:36,192 --> 00:27:38,595
earnestly pleading your love,

502
00:27:39,129 --> 00:27:41,831
she will be moved.

503
00:27:43,500 --> 00:27:45,235
CYRANO DE BERGERAC

504
00:27:45,301 --> 00:27:47,170
Ms. Kotone Wakatsuki!

505
00:27:47,704 --> 00:27:49,105
Can you hear me?

506
00:27:50,106 --> 00:27:50,940
No.

507
00:27:51,608 --> 00:27:53,877
Kotone, can you hear me?

508
00:28:02,352 --> 00:28:03,620
Wait, what are you doing?

509
00:28:03,686 --> 00:28:05,722
I have a dream.

510
00:28:06,689 --> 00:28:10,093
To one day become
the UN Secretary-General.

511
00:28:10,994 --> 00:28:12,695
I want to change the world.

512
00:28:12,762 --> 00:28:16,866
I want to create a world that does not
tolerate populism or discrimination.

513
00:28:17,433 --> 00:28:20,703
A world where people don't yearn
for narrow-minded nationalism,

514
00:28:20,770 --> 00:28:23,573
and instead atone
for the foolish, bloody history

515
00:28:23,640 --> 00:28:25,475
that we humans have created so far!

516
00:28:26,676 --> 00:28:28,144
I'm sorry, I don't understand.

517
00:28:28,211 --> 00:28:29,112
Well…

518
00:28:30,613 --> 00:28:31,781
I mean…

519
00:28:32,448 --> 00:28:33,283
Hey!

520
00:28:33,349 --> 00:28:35,118
-What I mean is…
-Now's the time! Go!

521
00:28:35,185 --> 00:28:36,052
Yes!

522
00:28:36,886 --> 00:28:38,454
-Now!
-Okay!

523
00:28:45,128 --> 00:28:46,896
Cyrano de Bergerac

524
00:28:47,964 --> 00:28:50,567
was ultimately never united
with his beloved Roxane,

525
00:28:51,367 --> 00:28:55,839
but even so, without losing heart,
he said two lines, which I love!

526
00:28:56,406 --> 00:28:57,574
The first one is,

527
00:28:57,640 --> 00:28:58,741
"To sing,

528
00:28:59,909 --> 00:29:01,678
to dream, to laugh,

529
00:29:02,245 --> 00:29:05,849
to walk, to be alone, be free…"

530
00:29:08,618 --> 00:29:10,987
He actually read the book!

531
00:29:11,054 --> 00:29:13,323
Nice one, Ayumu!

532
00:29:13,823 --> 00:29:15,191
The other one

533
00:29:16,326 --> 00:29:18,928
is the line Cyrano says
to Roxane at the very end.

534
00:29:20,730 --> 00:29:25,001
"There's one thing I will take with me
as I leave this world, and that is…"

535
00:29:25,068 --> 00:29:27,036
"My panache."

536
00:29:32,575 --> 00:29:33,743
Please!

537
00:29:34,310 --> 00:29:35,144
Kotone!

538
00:29:42,685 --> 00:29:43,686
What?

539
00:29:46,189 --> 00:29:47,090
Huh?

540
00:29:47,156 --> 00:29:48,791
It's you, Onicchi! What are you doing?

541
00:29:49,359 --> 00:29:51,361
Oh! This is just like that time!

542
00:29:51,427 --> 00:29:54,964
When Kikuchi didn't come to school,
we made it rain!

543
00:29:55,031 --> 00:29:57,967
How nostalgic! Whoa! Watch out!

544
00:29:58,534 --> 00:30:00,036
-Sorry!
-You idiot.

545
00:30:00,103 --> 00:30:01,938
-Onicchi, you okay?
-You!

546
00:30:02,005 --> 00:30:02,805
Stop it!

547
00:30:02,872 --> 00:30:04,974
-It's so cold!
-Stop it!

548
00:30:05,041 --> 00:30:07,043
Don't spray me!

549
00:30:07,110 --> 00:30:09,178
Watch out! Hey!

550
00:30:09,245 --> 00:30:10,546
Don't ever speak to me again!

551
00:30:17,053 --> 00:30:19,422
STAFF ROOM

552
00:30:19,989 --> 00:30:23,960
Onizuka, as usual,
what on earth were you thinking?

553
00:30:24,861 --> 00:30:27,297
The Principal has been apologizing

554
00:30:27,363 --> 00:30:30,066
to Kotone Wakatsuki's mother
for a while now.

555
00:30:30,133 --> 00:30:33,136
I apologized to her yesterday too.

556
00:30:33,202 --> 00:30:34,671
And that's not all.

557
00:30:35,505 --> 00:30:36,539
Look at this.

558
00:30:38,975 --> 00:30:43,046
Because of you, Ayumu Yoshida
is getting bashed online too.

559
00:30:43,112 --> 00:30:45,715
"His dream is to be Secretary-General?"

560
00:30:45,782 --> 00:30:48,251
"He can't do it, that damn stalker."

561
00:30:48,318 --> 00:30:52,221
Never mind me, but they
can't say such things to Ayumu!

562
00:30:52,288 --> 00:30:54,257
I'll find who wrote this
and teach them a lesson!

563
00:30:54,324 --> 00:30:55,525
Teach them a lesson?

564
00:30:56,092 --> 00:30:58,094
I told you!

565
00:30:59,629 --> 00:31:02,198
If you do that,
it will make the problem bigger,

566
00:31:02,265 --> 00:31:04,000
and it will just cause trouble for us!

567
00:31:05,034 --> 00:31:07,003
Why haven't you gotten it
through your head yet?

568
00:31:07,070 --> 00:31:11,808
Everything you say and do
is problematic in this era!

569
00:31:11,874 --> 00:31:14,477
Ryunosuke has made
countless women cry in the past.

570
00:31:14,544 --> 00:31:16,612
Ms. Koizumi, are you a single mother?

571
00:31:16,679 --> 00:31:18,815
Mr. Abe, have you never
dated anyone before?

572
00:31:19,849 --> 00:31:22,018
No way, are all of those off-limits?

573
00:31:25,188 --> 00:31:30,560
It's problematic for a teacher
to meddle in student romances!

574
00:31:31,828 --> 00:31:35,565
You understand now, right?
Don't do unnecessary things anymore!

575
00:31:38,267 --> 00:31:40,837
I've told him so many times…

576
00:31:42,305 --> 00:31:45,942
Ms. Kashiwabara, do you also agree
with what the vice-principal said?

577
00:31:46,576 --> 00:31:51,014
I don't think in this era, someone
like you can keep being a teacher.

578
00:31:51,080 --> 00:31:53,483
Even so, I think it's amazing
that you keep trying.

579
00:31:54,517 --> 00:31:58,054
Is that a compliment?
Or are you insulting me?

580
00:31:58,121 --> 00:32:00,957
I'm just interested to see
what you'll do next.

581
00:32:02,025 --> 00:32:04,193
Oh, okay.

582
00:32:05,595 --> 00:32:07,196
Good morning.

583
00:32:07,263 --> 00:32:08,631
Good morning.

584
00:32:08,698 --> 00:32:11,000
Good morning.

585
00:32:16,339 --> 00:32:18,508
About Mr. Ayumu…

586
00:32:20,710 --> 00:32:24,514
I just, you know, wanted to support him,

587
00:32:24,580 --> 00:32:28,518
and I would have done the same thing
for anyone in this class.

588
00:32:29,152 --> 00:32:32,822
Because, you know,
I want everyone to enjoy their youth.

589
00:32:41,564 --> 00:32:42,832
All right, I get it.

590
00:32:46,536 --> 00:32:49,605
If you all want to pretend
I don't exist, go ahead and try.

591
00:32:50,173 --> 00:32:53,609
But, Ayumu truly likes Kotone.

592
00:32:54,343 --> 00:32:58,047
He just summoned the courage
to convey his massive dream.

593
00:32:59,215 --> 00:33:04,387
I won't forgive anyone who makes fun
of his feelings and hurts him.

594
00:33:04,454 --> 00:33:06,923
I didn't write those posts.

595
00:33:06,989 --> 00:33:10,660
But everyone was asking me,
so I talked about it a little.

596
00:33:11,727 --> 00:33:15,098
Besides, it has only been
two months since we met.

597
00:33:15,164 --> 00:33:16,532
What does he actually know about me?

598
00:33:17,700 --> 00:33:19,135
We haven't even talked much.

599
00:33:19,202 --> 00:33:21,771
When someone likes me
just because of looks,

600
00:33:21,838 --> 00:33:23,072
it's just a pain.

601
00:33:23,139 --> 00:33:26,442
He didn't like you
just because of your looks.

602
00:33:27,310 --> 00:33:28,144
What?

603
00:33:28,711 --> 00:33:32,882
He respects the fact
that you greet adults properly

604
00:33:32,949 --> 00:33:34,750
and that you're kind to everyone.

605
00:33:35,351 --> 00:33:36,886
He truly admires that about you.

606
00:33:37,887 --> 00:33:42,692
That's why
he fell in love with you, Kotone.

607
00:33:49,999 --> 00:33:53,569
If there's anyone here
who wrote those posts online,

608
00:33:54,170 --> 00:33:57,940
know that he gathered his courage
and expressed his feelings,

609
00:33:58,007 --> 00:34:00,910
so don't dismiss him
and judge him by his cover!

610
00:34:01,811 --> 00:34:03,079
He…

611
00:34:04,213 --> 00:34:06,048
isn't a stalker or a fool.

612
00:34:06,115 --> 00:34:08,584
The reason he confessed his love

613
00:34:08,651 --> 00:34:11,053
was because he wanted
to make the person he loves happy!

614
00:34:11,120 --> 00:34:13,022
He held that dream

615
00:34:13,089 --> 00:34:16,592
because he wants
to save everyone in the world!

616
00:34:16,659 --> 00:34:19,095
What on earth is wrong with that?

617
00:34:19,162 --> 00:34:20,930
Calm down, Mr. Onizuka.

618
00:34:39,482 --> 00:34:40,316
<i>Yes?</i>

619
00:34:41,851 --> 00:34:45,321
I'm Onizuka, Ayumu's homeroom teacher.

620
00:34:45,388 --> 00:34:47,657
Is your son home?

621
00:34:47,723 --> 00:34:48,558
<i>What?</i>

622
00:34:48,624 --> 00:34:51,627
<i>Ayumu hasn't come home from school yet.</i>

623
00:34:52,862 --> 00:34:53,696
What?

624
00:35:26,562 --> 00:35:29,298
SUMMER LESSONS
UP YOUR GRADES AND MOTIVATION!

625
00:35:30,166 --> 00:35:32,101
Ms. Ayano.

626
00:35:32,802 --> 00:35:34,370
Have you seen Ayumu?

627
00:35:34,437 --> 00:35:36,439
No, did something happen?

628
00:35:37,139 --> 00:35:41,110
It looks like he lied to his parents today
about going to school.

629
00:35:41,177 --> 00:35:42,478
I see.

630
00:35:44,480 --> 00:35:45,314
Huh?

631
00:35:57,827 --> 00:35:59,028
Oh!

632
00:35:59,095 --> 00:36:01,497
Soma! What are you doing here?

633
00:36:01,564 --> 00:36:04,066
What's with you? You look so panicked.

634
00:36:04,734 --> 00:36:08,304
Ayumu is missing.
Let me know if you spot him.

635
00:36:08,371 --> 00:36:09,372
-Oh.
-What?

636
00:36:10,573 --> 00:36:11,807
I saw him a while ago.

637
00:36:12,541 --> 00:36:13,442
What?

638
00:36:22,752 --> 00:36:23,719
Ayumu?

639
00:36:29,158 --> 00:36:30,159
Hey!

640
00:36:30,226 --> 00:36:33,296
Ayumu, stop! Don't do anything stupid!

641
00:36:40,936 --> 00:36:41,837
What are you doing?

642
00:36:42,471 --> 00:36:44,140
What about you?

643
00:36:44,206 --> 00:36:46,509
I dropped my earphone,
I was looking for it.

644
00:36:46,575 --> 00:36:47,410
What?

645
00:36:53,215 --> 00:36:54,116
Damn it.

646
00:36:54,717 --> 00:36:56,619
I thought you were going to die.

647
00:36:57,320 --> 00:36:59,622
You skipped school,
and didn't tell your parents.

648
00:37:03,292 --> 00:37:04,126
Hey.

649
00:37:14,270 --> 00:37:16,372
I was planning on going back tomorrow.

650
00:37:17,106 --> 00:37:19,375
And besides, I can't afford to die.

651
00:37:20,109 --> 00:37:21,077
Why?

652
00:37:21,844 --> 00:37:23,012
Because…

653
00:37:23,079 --> 00:37:24,680
If I died, Kotone would be hurt, right?

654
00:37:29,185 --> 00:37:33,122
For her sake too,
I think I have to be my usual self.

655
00:37:34,123 --> 00:37:38,527
So I thought I'd just spend today
crying my eyes out all by myself.

656
00:37:40,963 --> 00:37:41,964
Ayumu.

657
00:37:43,132 --> 00:37:45,534
You really are amazing.

658
00:37:46,102 --> 00:37:46,869
What?

659
00:37:47,470 --> 00:37:50,706
Don't ever change
that part about yourself.

660
00:37:52,742 --> 00:37:55,177
And your dream of becoming
Secretary-General.

661
00:37:55,978 --> 00:37:57,613
Oh, I gave up on that.

662
00:37:58,614 --> 00:37:59,482
Why?

663
00:37:59,548 --> 00:38:03,085
I figured it's better to be
a bit more realistic.

664
00:38:04,220 --> 00:38:05,121
What?

665
00:38:05,187 --> 00:38:08,023
When I looked at the ranking
of jobs high schoolers want to have,

666
00:38:08,090 --> 00:38:11,494
customer service ranking first
or sales ranking fifth seem better to me.

667
00:38:11,560 --> 00:38:14,363
What's up with that?

668
00:38:16,499 --> 00:38:21,404
I know you're kind to people,
and I know you think things through.

669
00:38:22,505 --> 00:38:26,175
But why are you so hard on yourself?

670
00:38:26,876 --> 00:38:29,478
Why aren't you
expecting more from yourself?

671
00:38:33,849 --> 00:38:35,184
Times like these,

672
00:38:35,684 --> 00:38:39,822
you shouldn't be crying by yourself.
You just have to go wild and blow it off.

673
00:38:39,889 --> 00:38:41,157
Isn't there something?

674
00:38:41,223 --> 00:38:44,727
Something you
usually do to relieve stress.

675
00:38:48,531 --> 00:38:49,532
Do I have something?

676
00:38:50,065 --> 00:38:51,634
Yeah.

677
00:38:52,468 --> 00:38:53,836
Onicchi, sorry we're late!

678
00:38:53,903 --> 00:38:55,504
All right, let's have fun today!

679
00:38:55,571 --> 00:38:56,772
Yeah!

680
00:38:57,540 --> 00:38:58,541
Four people!

681
00:38:58,607 --> 00:38:59,675
I'm terribly sorry.

682
00:38:59,742 --> 00:39:01,977
We're currently full,
so it's a two-hour wait.

683
00:39:02,044 --> 00:39:03,446
-Really?
-What?

684
00:39:03,512 --> 00:39:05,481
Can't you do something about it, please?

685
00:39:05,548 --> 00:39:07,183
It's a real drag.

686
00:39:09,819 --> 00:39:13,022
Today is a party to cheer
this guy up, so please.

687
00:39:13,088 --> 00:39:14,256
I am terribly sorry.

688
00:39:14,323 --> 00:39:15,991
The heck you mean, "real drag"?

689
00:39:18,194 --> 00:39:19,428
Look at that.

690
00:39:20,062 --> 00:39:21,330
-Oh, what?
-Hey!

691
00:39:23,632 --> 00:39:24,733
Oh!

692
00:39:25,734 --> 00:39:27,369
She ran away!

693
00:39:27,436 --> 00:39:29,338
She's running away!

694
00:39:30,706 --> 00:39:33,476
Ms. Kashiwabara! What are you doing?

695
00:39:33,542 --> 00:39:35,411
Please open up!

696
00:39:37,480 --> 00:39:39,882
Oh! Ms. Kashiwabara, you're by yourself?

697
00:39:39,949 --> 00:39:40,783
A solo customer!

698
00:39:40,850 --> 00:39:42,051
She's a solo customer!

699
00:39:42,117 --> 00:39:45,821
I just come here by myself sometimes.
I can eat food and do some work here.

700
00:39:45,888 --> 00:39:48,691
Could it be you got your heart broken?

701
00:39:48,757 --> 00:39:49,859
Really?

702
00:39:52,595 --> 00:39:55,431
Wow. Nothing but breakup songs
in the history.

703
00:39:55,498 --> 00:39:59,502
That's because I've never been
heartbroken, so I was doing research.

704
00:39:59,568 --> 00:40:01,437
Oh, how annoying!

705
00:40:05,341 --> 00:40:06,208
Who is it?

706
00:40:06,275 --> 00:40:07,443
What?

707
00:40:49,585 --> 00:40:52,354
<i>I'll tell you!</i>

708
00:40:52,421 --> 00:40:54,456
<i>I'll tell you, Ayumu Yoshida!</i>

709
00:40:55,024 --> 00:40:59,028
<i>Hang in there! Can you hear me?</i>

710
00:40:59,094 --> 00:41:02,531
Hang in there!

711
00:41:10,806 --> 00:41:12,041
I got rejected.

712
00:41:16,445 --> 00:41:17,913
It was my first love.

713
00:41:23,285 --> 00:41:24,687
I really loved her.

714
00:41:33,596 --> 00:41:35,164
Heartbreak…

715
00:41:38,601 --> 00:41:39,702
It hurts…

716
00:41:42,304 --> 00:41:44,139
this much?

717
00:41:44,840 --> 00:41:46,041
Mr. Onizuka.

718
00:41:54,283 --> 00:41:55,217
Ayumu,

719
00:41:57,753 --> 00:41:58,821
today,

720
00:42:00,489 --> 00:42:04,460
you felt a feeling
you didn't know until yesterday.

721
00:42:06,528 --> 00:42:09,231
There's a word for that.

722
00:42:11,600 --> 00:42:12,568
What is it?

723
00:42:12,635 --> 00:42:15,504
Well, people call it…

724
00:42:15,571 --> 00:42:16,805
Right, Ms. Kashiwabara?

725
00:42:17,806 --> 00:42:19,608
Growth?

726
00:42:20,342 --> 00:42:21,410
Yes, exactly.

727
00:42:25,047 --> 00:42:26,281
You are

728
00:42:28,884 --> 00:42:30,019
growing right now.

729
00:42:44,400 --> 00:42:45,234
Hey.

730
00:42:45,968 --> 00:42:46,969
Want to take a BeReal?

731
00:42:47,036 --> 00:42:49,672
Oh, sounds good! Wait, what is that?

732
00:42:49,738 --> 00:42:50,873
Come on over.

733
00:42:50,939 --> 00:42:53,442
Okay, let's go.

734
00:42:59,481 --> 00:43:01,517
All right, cheese!

735
00:43:29,878 --> 00:43:31,780
Please let me say just two things.

736
00:43:32,347 --> 00:43:33,415
What is it?

737
00:43:34,283 --> 00:43:35,350
First,

738
00:43:36,685 --> 00:43:38,420
please don't get sick.

739
00:43:39,254 --> 00:43:43,325
It's going to get hotter from now on,
so please watch out for heatstroke.

740
00:43:45,961 --> 00:43:47,262
And the other thing?

741
00:43:48,363 --> 00:43:50,632
Find someone nice.

742
00:43:55,003 --> 00:43:56,205
Thank you.

743
00:43:59,108 --> 00:44:00,242
I'm sorry.

744
00:44:02,711 --> 00:44:03,879
Don't worry about it!

745
00:44:15,524 --> 00:44:17,559
All right, everyone to your seats.

746
00:44:20,929 --> 00:44:24,233
Now that Ayumu is here,
our class is a perfect number.

747
00:44:25,467 --> 00:44:26,869
-Mr. Onizuka.
-Yes?

748
00:44:26,935 --> 00:44:27,770
What's up?

749
00:44:29,204 --> 00:44:32,341
Please make my nickname
"Secretary-General."

750
00:44:34,276 --> 00:44:37,246
Understood. Secretary-General.

751
00:44:44,486 --> 00:44:47,356
All right, let's start homeroom!

752
00:44:53,996 --> 00:44:55,864
YOUR STUDIES

753
00:44:55,931 --> 00:45:00,002
ONIZUKA NEEDS TO BE PUNISHED SOON

754
00:45:00,569 --> 00:45:02,704
<i>I wish he'd disappear soon.</i>

755
00:45:02,771 --> 00:45:04,339
<i>What did you do now?</i>

756
00:45:04,406 --> 00:45:06,041
<i>-If you can't, you're fired!</i>
-It's been real.

757
00:45:06,108 --> 00:45:07,142
-What?
-What?

758
00:45:07,209 --> 00:45:10,012
<i>She left a note saying</i>
<i>she's running away, now she's gone.</i>

759
00:45:10,078 --> 00:45:12,414
Why don't you try finding
your own way of doing things?

760
00:45:12,481 --> 00:45:15,617
<i>Your classes are famous</i>
<i>for being boring, Mr. Murayama.</i>

761
00:45:15,684 --> 00:45:17,820
<i>Why don't you try doing something new?</i>

762
00:45:17,886 --> 00:45:19,421
<i>Isn't that a bit too harsh?</i>

763
00:45:19,488 --> 00:45:22,958
<i>I'm sure this time,</i>
<i>even your company will understand!</i>

764
00:45:23,025 --> 00:45:25,027
<i>Make my family laugh.</i>

765
00:45:26,295 --> 00:45:27,496
Happy bday.

766
00:45:28,096 --> 00:45:29,064
Subtitle translation by: Nix S.

